        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): preserve ANSI sanitizer state across bash chunks",
        "body": "Closes #103668\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen bash output splits ANSI/OSC controls across stdout callbacks, stateless per-chunk stripping can leak control fragments into streamed output, final results, and spill files.\n\nThe patch adds a bounded incremental terminal-core sanitizer and preserves one instance for each bash command. One-shot stripping remains unchanged while streamed output becomes callback-boundary invariant.\n\n## Evidence\n\nExact rebased head: `b2eda7bc13702ac3c680838ec8cfca52c6615e9d`\n\n- Focused Vitest passed: 3 files / 51 tests across 2 shards.\n- Direct changed-file lint, formatting, and `git diff --check upstream/main...HEAD` passed.\n- Real `executeBashWithOperations()` child-process coverage verifies clean split streamed chunks, final `ABCDEFGH`, and sanitized spill-file output.\n",
